<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Group Five shares fall as chief exec quits.</title>
<headline>Group Five shares fall as chief exec quits.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in South African building and construction products firm Group Five Ltd fell on Tuesday after news that the company's chief executive officer Theunis Kotzee had resigned, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 0955 GMT the stock had lost 20 cents to reach 830 cents.</p>
<p>&quot;They are down and that's (the resignation) probably the reason why,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>Group Five Ltd said on Tuesday Kotzee had announced his resignation following policy differences with the board.</p>
<p>It said Stan Goldstein, Group Five's chairman, will assume executive responsibilities until a new appointment is made.</p>
<p>The company gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Ellis Mnyandu, Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
